From: Dominique Leuenberger <dimstar@opensuse.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drop .INTERMEDIATE target for automake 1.20 compatibility

Automake 1.20 defines the internal make target .INTERMEDIATE in distdir.am.
Defining .INTERMEDIATE in Makefile.am causes automake to issue an override
warning, which fails the build under AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE([-Wall -Werror]).
---
 Makefile.am | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -45,7 +45,6 @@ EXTRA_DIST = linux/GitVersion.sh linux/P
 man_MANS = docs/sedutil-cli.8
 linux/Version.h:
 	$(srcdir)/linux/GitVersion.sh > linux/Version.h
-.INTERMEDIATE: linux/Version.h
 maintainer-clean-local:
 	rm config.status configure config.log
 	rm Makefile
